Subject: Refuse a <use> that references its own ancestor

render_use() points the referenced element's parent at the <use> while it
renders it. When the <use> is inside the element it references -- a
<symbol id="s"> holding <use href="#s"/>, found by zusvg's fuzzer -- that
makes the parent chain a loop (s -> use -> s), and find_attribute()'s
inheritance walk never ends. has_cycle_reference() looks only at the
render stack, so the first pass through such a <use> is not caught. The
render step budget counts render_element() calls and does not see the
loop either.

Walk the <use>'s ancestors before rewriting the pointer, and render
nothing when the referenced element is among them, as SVG 1.1 section 5.6
treats a circular reference.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §9. Offered upstream.

--- a/plutosvg/source/plutosvg.c
+++ b/plutosvg/source/plutosvg.c
@@ -2209,6 +2209,14 @@
     element_t* ref = resolve_href(context->document, element);
     if(ref == NULL)
         return;
+    /* A <use> of its own ancestor (or of itself) is a circular reference:
+     * rewriting ref->parent below would make the parent chain a loop, which
+     * attribute inheritance then walks forever. */
+    for(const element_t* p = element; p; p = p->parent) {
+        if(p == ref) {
+            return;
+        }
+    }
     length_t x = {0, length_type_fixed};
     length_t y = {0, length_type_fixed};
 
